    "title": "Session events: Add oversized payload guardrails with externalized blob pointers",
    "type": "bug",
    "description": "Problem: large ACP updates can inflate JSONL event lines and memory pressure. We need safety limits without losing auditability.\n\nScope (steps 3-4):\n1) Add framing/event safety caps (line/payload size) to prevent single-message heap blowups.\n2) For oversized payload fields (toolResponse stdout/stderr, rawOutput, large chunk text), write full content to session blob files under .kspec/sessions/<id>/blobs/.\n3) Store compact pointer objects in events.jsonl (path, bytes, sha256, truncated=true, preview).\n4) Update session log show/search behavior to surface previews by default and optionally resolve blob content on demand.\n\nNon-goal: silently dropping payloads. If payload is externalized, events must keep enough metadata to reconstruct/audit.",
