    "type": "task",
    "description": "**What**: After ralph merges PRs via the `pr-review-loop` workflow, remote branches accumulate because the merge step does not include `--delete-branch`. 13 stale branches were found after a single session. **Where**: `.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml` — the `pr-review-loop` workflow (id `01KFRX0S3VBZGV72A17E21AB9E`), specifically the merge action step at ~line 750-761 which references `kspec workflow start @pr-review-merge`. Also the `pr-review-merge` workflow merge step (~line 297-300) which says `gh pr merge (prefer merge commit to preserve trailers)`. The release skill at `.claude/skills/release/SKILL.md` line 220 already uses `gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch` as a pattern. **How**: Update the `pr-review-merge` workflow merge step content in `kynetic.meta.yaml` to explicitly include `--delete-branch` in the `gh pr merge` command guidance. Change the step from `gh pr merge (prefer merge commit to preserve trailers)` to `gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch`. This is a meta YAML change — use `kspec` CLI to update the workflow step, or edit the workflow directly. **Done when**: (1) The `pr-review-merge` workflow merge step includes `--delete-branch` in its guidance. (2) `kspec agents generate` regenerated to reflect the change. (3) After a ralph PR merge, the source branch is deleted from the remote.",
